=== Module 05 - Derivations, Parse Trees, Leftmost/Rightmost ===

grammar: fixtures/anbn.grammar
  (0) S -> a S b
  (1) S -> epsilon

target: a a b b

parse tree:
S
+- a
+- S
|  +- a
|  +- S
|  |  +- epsilon
|  +- b
+- b

yield (terminal frontier): a a b b
  matches target? true

leftmost derivation  (always expand the leftmost nonterminal):
    S
=>  a S b                   (S -> a S b)
=>  a a S b b               (S -> a S b)
=>  a a b b                 (S -> epsilon)
    3 steps

rightmost derivation  (always expand the rightmost nonterminal):
    S
=>  a S b                   (S -> a S b)
=>  a a S b b               (S -> a S b)
=>  a a b b                 (S -> epsilon)
    3 steps

productions used (multiset, sorted by index):
  leftmost : [S->aSb, S->aSb, S->eps]
  rightmost: [S->aSb, S->aSb, S->eps]
  same multiset? true  (they are derived from the SAME tree)

summary: parseTrees=1  canonicalDerivations=2  steps=3  productionsEach=3  sameMultiset=true
